{"availability":"available","full":"antonsoo/tracelens","name":"tracelens","description":"Zero-install viewer for LLM agent traces: OTLP or Jaeger JSON in, waterfall, span tree, tool calls, tokens and cost out.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-25T07:32:02Z","updated":"2026-10-11T06:56:27Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://antonsoo.github.io/tracelens/","topics":["agent-tracing","genai","llm-observability","openinference","opentelemetry","otlp","trace-viewer","typescript"],"demo":"https://antonsoo.github.io/tracelens/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:27:07.803Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:27:07.803Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:27:07.803Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:27:07.803Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A zero-install viewer for LLM agent traces. Drop an OpenTelemetry export, see every model call, tool call, token and dollar on a timeline.","Agent frameworks increasingly emit OpenTelemetry traces using the GenAI semantic conventions (genai. attributes) or Arize's OpenInference conventions. Viewing one of these traces today usually means standing up a server — Jaeger, Langfuse, Phoenix — for a file you could have opened locally. tracelens is a static, local-first web app plus a small CLI: point it at an OTLP/JSON trace file (or one downloaded from Jaeger) and get an agent-shaped waterfall, a span tree, per-span prompts and completions, tool calls, token usage and estimated cost, errors and retries, and a \"where did the time and…","Compare two runs to see which operations changed: elapsed time, calls, tokens, estimated cost and errors, with every aggregate linked back to its original spans. Repeated calls are grouped by operation path, so inserting a new model turn does not shift a guessed one-to-one alignment."],"features":["OTLP/JSON parser — resourceSpans → scopeSpans → spans, typed","A collector's file as it is written — the OpenTelemetry Collector's","file exporter writes JSON Lines, one export per batch, and every trace that passed through it. The lines are read as one export, and a file with several traces gets a picker (--trace in the CLI), opening on the trace…","Jaeger JSON too — a trace downloaded from the Jaeger UI is converted to","OTLP (microsecond times, typed tags, span kind and status from their tags, logs as events) and gets the same checks."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/antonsoo/tracelens/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4732f79a4b363bfa26090ff1d49075d54176107c574d915b37a5e65a8bcbd482","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T07:27:07.892Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:27:07.892Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A zero-install viewer for LLM agent traces. Drop an OpenTelemetry export, see every model call, tool call, token and dollar on a timeline.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/antonsoo/tracelens/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"Cache counts must be included in total input; billing details beyond the token price table are not modeled.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/antonsoo/tracelens/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"4732f79a4b363bfa26090ff1d49075d54176107c574d915b37a5e65a8bcbd482","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/antonsoo/tracelens/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:27:07.893Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-11T06:56:27Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/antonsoo/tracelens/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:27:07.895Z","hash":"4732f79a4b363bfa26090ff1d49075d54176107c574d915b37a5e65a8bcbd482","originalBytes":26745,"storedBytes":26745,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["trace","json","span","spans","run","tool","docs","npm","file","cost","tracelens","browser","cli","model","time","one","source","otlp","same","sdk","token","calls","example","comparison","